{"type":"text","timestamp":1794339992096,"sessionID":"ses_e390f5dcfffeIMyrnhIN59SkWV","part":{"id":"prt_1c6ff72080016F3MwxVOAIMc4p","messageID":"msg_1c6ff4fa4001WWw0MFlXM53ND7","sessionID":"ses_e390f5dcfffeIMyrnhIN59SkWV","type":"text","text":"Done. Summary of the implementation:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) — Flask + SQLite (`./data/app.db`, WAL):\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201; 400 invalid, 409 duplicate, `admin` reserved), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 `{\"token\": ...}`, Bearer-token auth elsewhere, 401 without a valid token)\n- Username lockout: 5 consecutive failed sign-ins → 429 with `Retry-After` for 15 min (even with the right password); success or admin unlock resets the count; expired locks reset too\n- Per-client limit: >20 login attempts/min → 429 with `Retry-After` (sliding 60s window keyed on `X-Forwarded-For`/remote addr)\n- `GET /api/me`, `GET /api/me/login-attempts` (20 newest, `at`/`success`), `GET /api/admin/locks`, `POST /api/admin/locks/{username}/unlock` (admin-only; 403 otherwise)\n- `admin` account's password comes from `ADMIN_PASSWORD` at start-up; unset/empty disables admin sign-in — no built-in password\n- Serves `frontend/dist` with SPA fallback; JSON 404s under `/api`\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`, React + TS + Vite + Tailwind v4): sign-in/registration forms, header with username + sign-out, 429 messages showing the server reason and \"try again after <time>\", account page (last sign-in + attempts history), admin page with Unlock buttons. `tsc --noEmit` and `vite build` both pass.\n\n**Dockerfile fix**: the template's `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` fails with modern pip (hash-pinned constraint files trigger `--require-hashes` but don't satisfy it), so it now installs the hash-pinned lock directly — verified with `pip install --require-hashes -r backend/requirements.lock`, `npm ci`, and a full gunicorn smoke test of every endpoint and rule.","time":{"start":1794339992072,"end":1794339992075}}}
